Regional Market Insights
•	North America: North America dominates the HFO-1234yf market, spearheaded by the United States where the EPA's SNAP program has driven widespread adoption since 2017. The region's mature automotive industry and well-established regulatory framework create a stable and high-demand environment.
•	Europe: Europe remains a critical and sophisticated market, having been an early adopter driven by the EU's F-Gas Regulation. The region maintains a strong focus on environmental sustainability, though it also experiences competitive pressure from R-744 systems in certain automotive segments.
•	Asia-Pacific: This region represents the fastest-growing market, fueled by massive automotive production in China, Japan, and South Korea. The pace of adoption varies, with advanced economies leading the transition while others follow as their national HFC phase-down plans gain momentum.
•	Latin America and the Middle East & Africa: These are developing markets primarily driven by the import of vehicles pre-equipped with HFO-1234yf systems. Growth is gradual, linked to the pace of local regulatory development and the build-out of service infrastructure.
